{
 "notes": ["VS MODE, the original's scene 44 (setup 0x04254b, the VS Scoobees read by 0x042428; entry 0x04183a, 0x04161f and 0x040aec; Scoobee select 0x042312, 0x0421b9 and 0x0418c6; area select 0x041778 and 0x0411ac; drawing 0x03ffc9 for the players' panels and 0x03fcc9 for the area select; static records 0x1fed30). The main menu's VS MODE opens it. Up to four players on the controller ports (0x0dee20) enter, each chooses a Scoobee, then the area is chosen and the battle starts (result 1, scene 6); leaving from the entry returns to the title's menu (result 0, scene 40).", "Ports: the keyboard is port 1 and the gamepads the ports after it (with four gamepads they take the four ports and the keyboard shares the first). Every port but the keyboard's shows No Controller while nothing is on it. The original's notice while no controller at all is connected (0x1fecbc) cannot show with the keyboard's port and is not ported.", "Panels (players[]): each player's panel grows from the corner nearest the screen's centre (grow_from; 0x0bbdb7's anchors) over panel.grow_seconds (20 frames), then its PLAYER label opens over panel.label_seconds (10); closing runs the other way. The panel is tinted joined_colour while the player has entered. What the panel shows (enter now or entered, the Scoobee strip, the chosen Scoobee, No Controller, No Entry) opens and closes over panel.open_seconds (10 frames), growing from its middle; the entry's next-step hint grows from the panel's edge (hint_from).", "Openings (popup): the black window and the phase's message (entry, select) grow over intro.grow_seconds (15 frames), stay until intro.shrink_from (75) and shrink until intro.end (90); from intro.shrink_from the panels open one after another intro.stagger (4 frames) apart. After intro.settle_seconds (30 frames) the players take input.", "Entry (0x040aec): confirm enters a player (sys 5); an entered player's confirm asks Are you ready? once two or more have entered (sys 5; with fewer it buzzes, sys 8). Cancel takes an entered player out (sys 8), or from one not entered leaves the VS mode (sys 8, the screen fading out over fade_out). The next-step hint shows on the entered players' panels while two or more have entered. Are you ready?: left/right choose (sys 4), cancel moves to NO (sys 4); YES closes the panels' contents one after another and turns to the Scoobee select after question.leave_seconds (46 frames); NO takes every player out again.", "Scoobee select (0x0418c6): each entered player chooses from their own strip: the three preset Scoobees (cards.presets, robots of tables/garage.json) and the kept VS Scoobees (KEEP SV), three cards shown at once (cards.visible) cards.step apart from cards_at, clipped to clip. Left/right move along them (sys 4); past the ends the strip scrolls by one over cards.scroll_seconds (8 frames), the cards pushed cards.push along at its half, the arrow that way lit. The name under the strip is the chosen card's. Confirm picks a preset or an undamaged kept Scoobee (sys 5): the panel's your SV! window opens with its icon and name. Cancel puts it back (sys 8); a player with a Scoobee picked buzzes on confirm. Once all have picked, Are you ready? asks: YES fades out to the area select, NO puts all the picks back. Cancel from a player still choosing asks whether to give up the play data (messages.abandon, NO chosen); YES returns to the entry.", "Wins and losses: each player's tally since the VS mode was entered (0x1107c and 0x1108c, three digits cards 13 apart); the battle's round-end menu adds each round to them (data/world/vs_battle.json).", "Area select (0x0411ac, drawn by 0x03fcc9 and the RUMBLING picture writer 0x015429): the backdrop, the strips, the picture frame and the bar (area_select.layers); the six items slide in from from_x over slide_seconds (24 frames, playing sys 44), the bar with EXIT. With crowd.players or more players only the crowd's items are there, at crowd.xs. Any entered player moves the cursor (sys 4); changing item cross-fades the pictures over fade_seconds (21 frames). Confirm on an area opens the time-zone window (0x1ffb1c, time_zone.grow_seconds, 12 frames): left/right choose DAY or NIGHT (sys 4; the picture cross-fades, the one not chosen dimmed to dim_colour), confirm starts the battle on the area's stage for that time, cancel closes it (sys 8). RANDOM starts a battle on a random stage (with a crowd only the arena's), its picture changing every random.every_seconds; EXIT fades back to the Scoobee select. Cancel moves to EXIT (sys 4).", "The battle: routes.battle with the stage (area * 2 + night, the original's 0x046674) and the players' Scoobees; see data/world/vs_battle.json. Coming back from it opens the area select again with the same players and Scoobees (the original's 0x4166e8 = 2), or after the battle's SELECT SV the Scoobee select."],
